1
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:18,670
I have to make it happen.

2
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:43,200
Hello? Okay, okay. I'll be right there.

3
00:01:43,770 --> 00:01:44,570
Mm-hmm.

4
00:02:02,330 --> 00:02:03,130
I'm here.

5
00:02:04,730 --> 00:02:05,530
Took you long enough.

6
00:02:06,470 --> 00:02:07,270
Sigh!

7
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:11,100
In an industry where everything changes faster than trends...

8
00:02:11,270 --> 00:02:12,070
Oh!

9
00:02:12,730 --> 00:02:13,530
What is it?

10
00:02:15,270 --> 00:02:16,070
Look at this.

11
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:19,600
Nannalin Thawarak.

12
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:24,170
Her name has become the talk of the fashion and publishing industries

13
00:02:24,170 --> 00:02:27,870
since she transformed the image of a long-established magazine

14
00:02:27,870 --> 00:02:30,630
and made it influential again in the digital age.

15
00:02:30,630 --> 00:02:32,000
Over the past two years...

16
00:02:32,570 --> 00:02:35,500
she has received rising executive awards from several institutions

17
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:38,570
for her leadership and for bringing print media

18
00:02:38,570 --> 00:02:40,700
back into the spotlight among younger generations.

19
00:02:40,970 --> 00:02:42,000
There's your witch.

20
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,100
She's in the news again.

21
00:02:43,570 --> 00:02:46,800
Don't call her a witch. She's gorgeous!

22
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:48,370
Why?

23
00:02:48,370 --> 00:02:49,370
What should I call her, then?

24
00:02:49,370 --> 00:02:51,530
The angel of the fashion industry?

25
00:02:55,530 --> 00:02:56,670
She's so cool!

26
00:02:58,370 --> 00:02:59,570
What's so cool about her?

27
00:02:59,570 --> 00:03:01,500
Seriously, what's cool?

28
00:03:02,870 --> 00:03:06,100
People fear her because she's brilliant.

29
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:09,730
That's quite a romantic way to justify being scary.

30
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:15,300
Namkhing, look! She's not just beautiful.

31
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:17,100
She's incredibly powerful.

32
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:20,930
It's like... wherever she goes, people have to listen.

33
00:03:21,730 --> 00:03:23,370
You're losing it.

34
00:03:24,570 --> 00:03:27,730
Just watch. One day, I'll be like her.

35
00:03:28,130 --> 00:03:28,870
Like what?

36
00:03:28,870 --> 00:03:29,730
Beautiful?

37
00:03:31,170 --> 00:03:32,100
You're already beautiful, honey.

38
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:35,630
I mean I'll be as capable as her, and...

39
00:03:35,630 --> 00:03:37,800
people will recognize me for my work.

40
00:03:38,570 --> 00:03:40,270
Here comes the inspirational speech.

41
00:03:40,530 --> 00:03:42,500
Oh, I've got goosebumps!

42
00:03:43,470 --> 00:03:44,270
Are you teasing me?

43
00:03:45,730 --> 00:03:47,430
No, I'm not.

44
00:03:47,430 --> 00:03:50,800
I'm so moved, I could cry.

45
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:51,470
Hey!

46
00:03:54,570 --> 00:03:55,770
But seriously,

47
00:03:55,770 --> 00:03:59,130
she's beautiful and talented. No argument there.

48
00:03:59,130 --> 00:04:02,330
Still, those rumors are pretty scary.

49
00:04:02,330 --> 00:04:03,400
You know, that she's...

50
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:04,200
ruthless.

51
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:05,770
A perfectionist about everything.

52
00:04:05,770 --> 00:04:07,600
If anyone messes up in front of her,

53
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:09,430
well...

54
00:04:09,430 --> 00:04:11,300
they practically won't survive at the office.

55
00:04:11,770 --> 00:04:14,200
Come on! Isn't that an exaggeration?

56
00:04:15,470 --> 00:04:16,430
I heard

57
00:04:16,430 --> 00:04:17,829
she's demanding, too.

58
00:04:17,829 --> 00:04:19,500
She always gets what she wants.

59
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:22,470
The work has to match exactly what she envisions.

60
00:04:25,070 --> 00:04:28,470
But what if what she wants actually improves the company?

61
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:30,970
Someone that capable

62
00:04:30,970 --> 00:04:34,330
can't be a sweet angel all the time, can she?

63
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:38,100
If she weren't so precise and detail-oriented,

64
00:04:38,100 --> 00:04:41,000
how could she lead such a huge company forward?

65
00:04:42,170 --> 00:04:42,970
Oh, please!

66
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:44,870
You've been hypnotized.

67
00:04:46,470 --> 00:04:48,270
I admire her, okay?

68
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:50,200
Okay.

69
00:04:50,570 --> 00:04:52,500
I'll stop teasing you, Miss Alice-

70
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:56,300
future powerhouse female executive.

71
00:04:58,970 --> 00:04:59,800
Just you wait.

72
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:01,500
Then wait and see.

73
00:05:05,100 --> 00:05:05,900
No need to watch anymore.

74
00:05:11,970 --> 00:05:12,830
Oh?

75
00:05:12,830 --> 00:05:15,330
Let's change the channel from female executives

76
00:05:15,330 --> 00:05:17,300
to your real-life girlfriend.

77
00:05:19,300 --> 00:05:20,300
Hello, Namhom?

78
00:05:21,130 --> 00:05:21,870
Alice.

79
00:05:21,870 --> 00:05:23,500
Can you come see me?

80
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:24,200
Right now.

81
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:25,900
Is something wrong?

82
00:05:26,370 --> 00:05:28,400
I just want you to be the first person I tell.

83
00:05:28,400 --> 00:05:29,770
That's all.

84
00:05:31,670 --> 00:05:32,470
Hey!

85
00:05:32,970 --> 00:05:33,800
Where are you going?

86
00:05:34,070 --> 00:05:35,300
Class is about to start!

87
00:05:35,770 --> 00:05:36,870
Take my handouts for me!

88
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:38,400
Hey! Hey!

89
00:05:39,170 --> 00:05:39,970
Hey!

90
00:05:40,100 --> 00:05:41,870
Am I your friend or your filing cabinet?

91
00:05:42,070 --> 00:05:43,670
You're my very best friend!

92
00:05:44,100 --> 00:05:44,900
Take this, too. Here!

93
00:05:53,130 --> 00:05:55,330
You sure run fast when it's for love.

94
00:06:04,070 --> 00:06:05,400
Namhom, what's wrong?

95
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:06,370
Why are you crying?

96
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:28,470
I passed the audition!

97
00:06:29,770 --> 00:06:30,570
Really?

98
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:31,400
Mm-hmm.

99
00:06:31,770 --> 00:06:34,470
See? I told you you'd make it, Namhom.

100
00:06:35,770 --> 00:06:36,570
At first,

101
00:06:37,570 --> 00:06:39,800
I was sure I wouldn't pass.

102
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:41,770
My hands were shaking,

103
00:06:41,770 --> 00:06:43,600
and my voice almost cracked.

104
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:46,470
But you passed! See?

105
00:06:46,470 --> 00:06:49,100
I told you you're amazing, Namhom.

106
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:53,870
You're the first person I've told, Alice.

107
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:56,970
From now on,

108
00:06:56,970 --> 00:06:58,770
you'll have to practice even harder.

109
00:06:58,770 --> 00:07:00,630
And eat your meals on time.

110
00:07:00,630 --> 00:07:01,770
No staying up late.

111
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:03,930
Got it?

112
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:06,500
You sound like a celebrity manager.

113
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:08,470
I could be one for you.

114
00:07:08,470 --> 00:07:10,730
When you become super famous,

115
00:07:10,730 --> 00:07:13,200
I'll tell everyone...

116
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:15,700
that I spotted your talent ages ago.

117
00:07:17,970 --> 00:07:19,770
Do you think I can do it, Alice?

118
00:07:21,870 --> 00:07:22,930
Of course you can.

119
00:07:22,930 --> 00:07:26,130
You're going to be a huge star, Namhom.

120
00:07:44,330 --> 00:07:45,700
What's wrong, Alice?

121
00:07:59,100 --> 00:08:00,330
They don't allow you to date?

122
00:08:02,170 --> 00:08:04,800
It's probably about the agency's image.

123
00:08:09,970 --> 00:08:10,770
But why?

124
00:08:12,570 --> 00:08:14,270
We're not doing anything wrong.

125
00:08:16,270 --> 00:08:17,730
I just love you, Alice.

126
00:08:21,130 --> 00:08:22,270
What's wrong with that?

127
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:27,600
Then I won't sign it.

128
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:28,770
That contract.

129
00:08:28,770 --> 00:08:29,470
Namhom.

130
00:08:34,070 --> 00:08:35,970
You earned this opportunity

131
00:08:37,070 --> 00:08:38,000
because you're talented.

132
00:08:41,669 --> 00:08:43,370
Please don't give it up for me.

133
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:47,400
I don't want to lose you, Alice.

134
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:54,900
I'm still right here.

135
00:08:56,900 --> 00:08:58,100
It's just that maybe...

136
00:08:58,100 --> 00:09:01,730
we'll have to be somewhere no one else can see us.

137
00:09:14,470 --> 00:09:16,170
That's so unfair.

138
00:09:20,770 --> 00:09:21,900
Yeah.

139
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:24,930
It really is unfair.

140
00:09:42,700 --> 00:09:44,000
I love you, Alice.

141
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:47,470
I love you too, Namhom.

142
00:09:49,530 --> 00:09:51,700
That's why I want you to follow your dream.

143
00:10:42,800 --> 00:10:44,600
Well, hello, girlfriend of the year!

144
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:46,930
Good news so big you had to call me?

145
00:10:53,370 --> 00:10:55,730
Yeah. It's really great.

146
00:10:57,470 --> 00:10:58,430
Alice,

147
00:10:58,430 --> 00:11:00,070
what happened?

148
00:11:03,870 --> 00:11:04,930
Are you free tonight?

149
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:07,000
Come hang out with me.

150
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:10,000
What's going on?

151
00:11:18,970 --> 00:11:20,300
Nothing.

152
00:11:20,300 --> 00:11:22,170
I just feel like drinking.

153
00:11:25,370 --> 00:11:27,770
Celebrating with a voice like you're about to cry?

154
00:11:29,070 --> 00:11:30,900
Alice, what's going on with Namhom?

155
00:11:36,130 --> 00:11:37,770
Namhom passed her audition.

156
00:11:39,130 --> 00:11:41,400
Isn't that amazing news?

157
00:11:43,930 --> 00:11:45,000
It's wonderful.

158
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:47,000
So wonderful that I have to...

159
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:49,270
be really, really happy for her, right?

160
00:11:51,270 --> 00:11:52,870
Where are you? I'll come to you.

161
00:11:55,970 --> 00:11:58,300
Aren't you busy with something?

162
00:11:58,830 --> 00:11:59,670
You don't need to come.

163
00:12:01,770 --> 00:12:03,070
I am busy,

164
00:12:03,070 --> 00:12:04,530
but if you're crying,

165
00:12:04,530 --> 00:12:05,530
I can drop everything.

166
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:09,900
Who's crying? I'm not crying!

167
00:12:12,470 --> 00:12:13,370
You...

168
00:12:13,370 --> 00:12:15,130
You're a terrible liar, yet you keep lying.

169
00:12:19,570 --> 00:12:21,470
I'll wait at our usual place.

170
00:12:21,470 --> 00:12:22,970
When you're done,

171
00:12:22,970 --> 00:12:24,330
come meet me there.

172
00:12:26,770 --> 00:12:28,700
Are you sure you'll be okay alone?

173
00:12:29,300 --> 00:12:30,230
Mm-hmm.

174
00:12:30,230 --> 00:12:31,830
I'm tough, remember?

175
00:12:34,070 --> 00:12:37,100
Okay, wait there. I'll join you soon.

176
00:12:37,100 --> 00:12:38,870
Don't drink too much before I get there.

177
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:41,000
Okay.

178
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:45,170
And... you don't have to be strong all the time.

179
00:12:45,170 --> 00:12:46,100
Understand?

180
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:48,800
Mm-hmm.

181
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:01,170
Sorry, something urgent came up.

182
00:14:01,370 --> 00:14:04,270
I'll be a little late.

183
00:14:46,470 --> 00:14:48,100
Isn't that Nannalin?

184
00:15:06,330 --> 00:15:07,400
Her zipper's open.

185
00:15:13,800 --> 00:15:14,930
Should I tell her?

186
00:15:30,130 --> 00:15:30,930
Sigh.

187
00:15:52,930 --> 00:15:53,730
Um...

188
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:56,800
Excuse me.

189
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:01,200
Excuse me.

190
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:13,900
Here goes nothing.

191
00:18:02,970 --> 00:18:09,070
Two years later.

192
00:18:44,730 --> 00:18:45,400
Okay.

193
00:19:08,900 --> 00:19:09,700
I'm here.

194
00:19:10,800 --> 00:19:13,200
Future content creator extraordinaire!

195
00:19:13,630 --> 00:19:14,870
Is your voice shaking?

196
00:19:15,170 --> 00:19:15,970
No.

197
00:19:17,400 --> 00:19:18,970
Well, maybe a little.

198
00:19:19,730 --> 00:19:22,470
Girl, you prepared a portfolio like you're taking over the company.

199
00:19:22,470 --> 00:19:23,200
Don't be scared.

200
00:19:23,870 --> 00:19:26,200
But I just graduated,

201
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:28,170
and I don't have any experience.

202
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:29,700
You've got brains,

203
00:19:29,700 --> 00:19:30,800
passion,

204
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:31,770
You've got a portfolio

205
00:19:31,770 --> 00:19:33,400
and superhuman determination.

206
00:19:33,700 --> 00:19:36,070
If they don't hire you, it's their loss.

207
00:19:36,600 --> 00:19:38,330
Yeah, thanks.

208
00:19:39,100 --> 00:19:40,200
And remember:

209
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:42,900
Don't panic. Don't apologize every three sentences.

210
00:19:42,900 --> 00:19:43,870
And...

211
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:45,400
What else?

212
00:19:45,870 --> 00:19:47,600
Be yourself as much as possible.

213
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:49,600
Your angel will always bless you.

214
00:19:50,370 --> 00:19:50,870
Got it!

215
00:19:50,870 --> 00:19:53,370
This time, I'm not backing down.

216
00:19:54,400 --> 00:19:55,200
Mm-hmm.

217
00:19:55,570 --> 00:19:56,370
Talk later.

218
00:20:17,170 --> 00:20:18,270
Aranya, right?

219
00:20:18,930 --> 00:20:19,730
Yes.

220
00:20:20,170 --> 00:20:20,970
This way.

221
00:20:23,800 --> 00:20:26,600
Slow down, slow down. Don't panic. Don't panic.

222
00:20:32,530 --> 00:20:33,900
Please give us a brief introduction.

223
00:20:34,470 --> 00:20:36,000
Um, hello.

224
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,530
I'm Aranya, but you can call me Alice.

225
00:20:38,530 --> 00:20:40,770
I graduated in marketing communications.

226
00:20:40,770 --> 00:20:43,370
I'm interested in fashion content

227
00:20:43,370 --> 00:20:46,000
and telling brand stories through people.

228
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:47,570
Um...

229
00:20:47,570 --> 00:20:51,230
I believe fashion isn't just about clothing.

230
00:20:51,230 --> 00:20:52,770
It's a language

231
00:20:52,770 --> 00:20:54,900
people use to express who they are,

232
00:20:55,900 --> 00:20:57,470
how they want others to see them,

233
00:20:58,070 --> 00:21:00,530
and how they shape the way they're perceived.

234
00:21:01,130 --> 00:21:02,100
That's an interesting idea.

235
00:21:02,770 --> 00:21:04,930
Did you do all of this yourself?

236
00:21:05,500 --> 00:21:06,170
Yes.

237
00:21:06,170 --> 00:21:08,900
It's a hypothetical brief for a perfume brand.

238
00:21:08,900 --> 00:21:14,230
I started by asking how a woman should feel walking into a meeting room.

239
00:21:14,230 --> 00:21:16,170
Then I worked out the mood,

240
00:21:16,170 --> 00:21:17,070
the message,

241
00:21:17,070 --> 00:21:19,930
and found KOLs who could communicate that feeling.

242
00:21:20,570 --> 00:21:23,170
You have a good understanding of brand image.

243
00:21:24,130 --> 00:21:24,900
Thank you.

244
00:21:25,300 --> 00:21:26,870
I think...

245
00:21:26,870 --> 00:21:29,970
products don't just sell features.

246
00:21:29,970 --> 00:21:33,900
They sell the feeling people want when they use them.

247
00:21:34,670 --> 00:21:35,930
But it's a high-pressure environment here.

248
00:21:36,730 --> 00:21:37,570
Briefs change quickly,

249
00:21:37,970 --> 00:21:38,870
clients request endless revisions,

250
00:21:39,370 --> 00:21:40,600
and KOLs are hard to coordinate with.

251
00:21:41,070 --> 00:21:42,270
Even work you think is already good

252
00:21:42,670 --> 00:21:44,570
might be revised beyond recognition.

253
00:21:49,930 --> 00:21:50,770
Is it "Clean Food"?

254
00:21:51,070 --> 00:21:53,070
It has to be clean because of the body requirements.

255
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:56,670
The legs... the legs are too big.

256
00:21:57,600 --> 00:21:59,100
Yes, the legs are too big.

257
00:22:10,970 --> 00:22:11,970
Here.

258
00:22:12,630 --> 00:22:14,070
I asked for the revised file,

259
00:22:14,070 --> 00:22:16,370
not excuses about why it isn't finished.

260
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:18,430
I forgot to send it.

261
00:22:18,430 --> 00:22:21,370
My partner had to be rushed to the hospital,

262
00:22:21,370 --> 00:22:23,870
and they have no family, so I...

263
00:22:24,300 --> 00:22:25,530
During work hours?

264
00:22:26,400 --> 00:22:27,200
Yes.

265
00:22:27,930 --> 00:22:29,430
That document

266
00:22:29,830 --> 00:22:32,300
forced the client team to attend a meeting

267
00:22:32,300 --> 00:22:34,670
without any confirmed information.

268
00:22:34,670 --> 00:22:37,830
Without it, the KOL team followed the wrong schedule,

269
00:22:37,830 --> 00:22:40,970
and the client thought we were unprepared.

270
00:22:44,570 --> 00:22:45,800
I'm really sorry.

271
00:22:46,930 --> 00:22:48,270
Your partner...

272
00:22:48,270 --> 00:22:50,500
still needs treatment for quite a while, right?

273
00:22:51,730 --> 00:22:53,600
Yes, for several weeks.

274
00:22:56,070 --> 00:22:57,600
Then go home.

275
00:22:57,600 --> 00:22:59,430
Go take care of them.

276
00:22:59,430 --> 00:23:02,130
And don't come back. Not for a very long time.

277
00:23:03,330 --> 00:23:04,600
Do you think you can handle it?

278
00:23:07,170 --> 00:23:07,970
I can.

279
00:23:08,330 --> 00:23:09,730
I may not be the best yet,

280
00:23:10,130 --> 00:23:12,130
but I'm not afraid to start from zero.

281
00:23:12,400 --> 00:23:13,470
And I'm not afraid of hard work.

282
00:23:14,400 --> 00:23:15,300
Something's happened!

283
00:23:15,970 --> 00:23:17,770
The witch just fired Jang!

284
00:23:18,600 --> 00:23:19,870
And that's not all.

285
00:23:19,870 --> 00:23:20,900
She said...

286
00:23:20,900 --> 00:23:22,870
she needs a new assistant by today.

287
00:23:24,070 --> 00:23:25,630
Today, no exceptions!

288
00:23:25,630 --> 00:23:29,200
I'll go check on Jang. I don't know if she's okay.

289
00:23:29,470 --> 00:23:31,700
Where are we supposed to find someone today?

290
00:23:36,530 --> 00:23:37,330
Unless...

291
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:39,000
What do you think?

292
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:40,100
Her portfolio is pretty good.

293
00:23:41,800 --> 00:23:42,900
Alice?

294
00:23:43,470 --> 00:23:45,000
Do you still want to work here,

295
00:23:45,670 --> 00:23:47,500
even if it's not in content creation?

296
00:23:48,370 --> 00:23:49,330
What position is it?

297
00:23:57,470 --> 00:23:58,800
Ms. Nannalin?

298
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:01,300
We've found someone.

299
00:24:03,370 --> 00:24:04,170
Mm.

300
00:24:04,600 --> 00:24:05,670
That was quick.

301
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:10,270
I just hope she's not useless,

302
00:24:10,870 --> 00:24:12,700
irresponsible,

303
00:24:12,700 --> 00:24:14,600
so obsessed with her partner that she ruins her work,

304
00:24:14,770 --> 00:24:16,730
or completely incompetent.

305
00:24:17,730 --> 00:24:19,770
I don't have time to train...

306
00:24:19,770 --> 00:24:23,300
people who can't separate work from their personal lives.

307
00:24:25,930 --> 00:24:28,030
This candidate is quite good, Ms. Nannalin.

308
00:24:28,030 --> 00:24:29,700
Her work is strong,

309
00:24:29,700 --> 00:24:30,900
her portfolio is solid,

310
00:24:31,230 --> 00:24:33,470
she understands branding,

311
00:24:33,470 --> 00:24:35,270
and she can write articles.

312
00:24:39,300 --> 00:24:40,270
Write articles?

313
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:42,800
Yes.

314
00:24:43,900 --> 00:24:46,300
She originally applied for the content creator position.

315
00:24:47,400 --> 00:24:49,500
Then why is she applying to be my assistant?

316
00:24:51,270 --> 00:24:52,200
Well...

317
00:24:52,200 --> 00:24:54,300
The thing is...

318
00:24:54,300 --> 00:24:57,130
our content creator position is already filled.

319
00:24:58,700 --> 00:25:00,800
The chairman's niece or nephew has taken the role.

320
00:25:02,370 --> 00:25:04,930
Of course.

321
00:25:07,170 --> 00:25:14,600
Give the content creator job to someone with connections, and send the person with real talent to be my assistant.

322
00:25:35,800 --> 00:25:36,770
Did she write this herself?

323
00:25:38,330 --> 00:25:40,770
Yes, I asked her questions,

324
00:25:41,700 --> 00:25:42,770
and she answered them. She definitely didn't memorize it.

325
00:25:43,200 --> 00:25:44,470
She definitely didn't memorize it.

326
00:25:49,870 --> 00:25:52,000
Are you all right, Ms. Nannalin?

327
00:25:56,000 --> 00:25:56,500
I'm fine.

328
00:25:57,930 --> 00:25:58,800
Send her in.

329
00:25:59,700 --> 00:26:00,500
Yes.

330
00:26:40,600 --> 00:26:42,070
Namkhing!

331
00:26:42,930 --> 00:26:44,270
Whoa!

332
00:26:44,970 --> 00:26:48,030
Well, look who finally decided to show up, Miss Busy Assistant!

333
00:26:48,030 --> 00:26:49,600
I thought they'd confiscated your phone.

334
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:51,400
I'm lucky I even escaped.

335
00:26:54,470 --> 00:26:55,700
But your face...

336
00:26:58,000 --> 00:27:00,570
doesn't look like someone celebrating a new job.

337
00:27:01,330 --> 00:27:02,270
What's wrong with my face?

338
00:27:04,530 --> 00:27:08,330
You look like someone's sucked your soul out.

339
00:27:08,770 --> 00:27:12,400
I thought it was your dream agency! Blessed by the heavens, huh?

340
00:27:13,500 --> 00:27:16,770
More like a nightmare of magnitude ten!

341
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:20,900
Oh! Is your boss really that scary?

342
00:27:22,730 --> 00:27:27,370
So scary I wanted to run away and become a nun on my first day!

343
00:27:30,670 --> 00:27:31,730
Okay, here's what we're doing.

344
00:27:32,430 --> 00:27:36,030
Tell me everything, starting from the second you stepped into the building.

345
00:27:36,030 --> 00:27:37,970
Don't leave out a single detail.

346
00:28:08,870 --> 00:28:11,170
Hello, I'm Aranya.

347
00:28:12,830 --> 00:28:15,070
You can call me Alice.

348
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:21,370
What do you think my assistant's responsibilities are?

349
00:28:25,330 --> 00:28:30,230
Um, organizing tasks, coordinating work, supporting decisions,

350
00:28:30,600 --> 00:28:32,800
and making the boss's job easier.

351
00:28:37,170 --> 00:28:38,900
That sounds straight out of a job interview handbook.

352
00:28:46,470 --> 00:28:48,270
Then may I try answering again?

353
00:28:49,600 --> 00:28:50,400
Go ahead.

354
00:28:54,000 --> 00:28:56,730
An assistant shouldn't just follow orders.

355
00:28:56,730 --> 00:28:59,800
They should know which issues need the boss's attention

356
00:28:59,800 --> 00:29:01,770
and which can be handled

357
00:29:02,170 --> 00:29:03,530
before they ever reach the boss.

358
00:29:03,530 --> 00:29:07,570
Remember the details and coordinate everything thoroughly.

359
00:29:07,570 --> 00:29:09,800
And when there's something they don't know,

360
00:29:09,800 --> 00:29:13,300
ask clearly the first time instead of wasting time asking again.

361
00:29:17,900 --> 00:29:21,000
And what if your boss is extremely demanding?

362
00:29:21,730 --> 00:29:26,500
Then I'd need to learn what's being unreasonable

363
00:29:26,500 --> 00:29:28,570
and what's simply a work standard.

364
00:29:46,500 --> 00:29:47,400
Do you know who I am?

365
00:29:52,070 --> 00:29:55,500
Yes, I've seen you in the news.

366
00:29:56,870 --> 00:29:57,970
In the news?

367
00:29:58,700 --> 00:29:59,600
Yes.

368
00:30:03,970 --> 00:30:05,130
What about anywhere else?

369
00:30:32,670 --> 00:30:35,670
Um, I'm sorry...

370
00:30:37,270 --> 00:30:41,600
I don't mean to be disrespectful, but I just noticed...

371
00:30:42,130 --> 00:30:45,700
your zipper had slipped down, so...

372
00:30:45,970 --> 00:30:48,500
I only wanted to zip it up for you.

373
00:30:49,170 --> 00:30:49,900
Um...

374
00:30:51,270 --> 00:30:54,300
I wasn't trying to look, I mean...

375
00:30:58,100 --> 00:31:01,100
I did look, but not in that way!

376
00:31:06,200 --> 00:31:10,530
Do you often help strangers like this?

377
00:31:12,070 --> 00:31:14,300
No! This is the first time.

378
00:31:14,970 --> 00:31:19,800
I mean, my first time zipping up a stranger's clothes.

379
00:31:20,500 --> 00:31:21,930
Not my first time helping someone.

380
00:31:23,700 --> 00:31:28,200
I usually help people in more normal ways.

381
00:31:32,170 --> 00:31:32,830
Well, then...

382
00:31:34,230 --> 00:31:37,670
go ahead and finish zipping it up.

383
00:31:41,970 --> 00:31:42,770
Yes.

384
00:32:02,270 --> 00:32:03,400
Is something wrong with the outfit?

385
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:08,070
Oh, no.

386
00:32:19,970 --> 00:32:21,870
Actually, maybe a little.

387
00:32:49,170 --> 00:32:50,100
All done.

388
00:32:53,530 --> 00:32:54,330
Thank you.

389
00:32:56,970 --> 00:32:57,700
You're welcome.

390
00:32:57,700 --> 00:32:58,500
Um...

391
00:32:58,570 --> 00:32:59,870
I'm sorry again.

392
00:33:03,800 --> 00:33:04,930
You apologize a lot.

393
00:33:08,300 --> 00:33:13,900
Well, I've gotten so many things wrong today.

394
00:33:15,300 --> 00:33:20,600
Next time you want to help someone, ask first.

395
00:33:25,670 --> 00:33:27,270
Yes, I'll remember that.

396
00:33:33,970 --> 00:33:34,770
Good.

397
00:38:56,070 --> 00:39:01,330
Um, a lot of people talk about you.

398
00:39:12,470 --> 00:39:15,670
If you're ready to start, read this in ten minutes.

399
00:39:15,970 --> 00:39:16,770
Huh?

400
00:39:17,130 --> 00:39:21,100
Then summarize what's holding this campaign back,

401
00:39:21,100 --> 00:39:25,670
who's responsible for what, and what needs fixing before noon.

402
00:39:28,170 --> 00:39:28,970
Of course.

403
00:39:30,370 --> 00:39:31,500
Any questions?

404
00:39:33,270 --> 00:39:36,500
Um, could I get access to the dashboard?

405
00:39:36,500 --> 00:39:40,070
I don't think this document alone will show the underlying issues.

406
00:39:41,100 --> 00:39:42,500
Ask the data team.

407
00:39:44,130 --> 00:39:44,930
Yes.

408
00:39:46,270 --> 00:39:47,900
Oh, and Alice.

409
00:39:48,600 --> 00:39:49,400
Yes?

410
00:39:50,470 --> 00:39:52,370
Next time you want to help me,

411
00:39:53,570 --> 00:39:55,200
ask me first.

412
00:39:57,300 --> 00:39:58,100
Of course.

413
00:39:59,700 --> 00:40:00,500
Good.

414
00:40:37,370 --> 00:40:38,170
Excuse me.

415
00:40:38,970 --> 00:40:40,800
Are you going to stand there all day?

416
00:40:41,100 --> 00:40:41,900
Sorry!

417
00:40:42,130 --> 00:40:43,330
Your heart's beating so fast.

418
00:40:43,670 --> 00:40:44,530
Just like that night.

419
00:40:45,370 --> 00:40:47,570
That lipstick looks good on you.

420
00:40:47,970 --> 00:40:49,800
Does this still count as teaching me?

421
00:40:50,130 --> 00:40:52,370
My boss is just too beautiful.

422
00:40:53,000 --> 00:40:57,870
Beautiful? Since when is 'too beautiful' part of the job title, Miss Assistant?

423
00:40:58,100 --> 00:40:59,870
Well? What do you think? Does it work?

424
00:41:00,270 --> 00:41:03,070
Do you have a date, or is there a special occasion?

425
00:41:03,370 --> 00:41:05,770
Ms. Rinrada, is there something urgent?

426
00:41:06,500 --> 00:41:11,700
I'm worried this woman has some hidden agenda behind all that advertising money.
